WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.040
- All right, I always love to close out

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.480
with something fun and inspiring.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.715
This is "#What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.715 --> 00:00:07.350
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.970
Earlier this year we had P!nk here

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.700
for a whole hour, because why not?

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.720
I love her.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.040
We also featured an artist

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.170
that she worked with named Tim Wakefield.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.320
He creates one of a kind
pieces depicted in sound waves,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.050
and he auctions them off
for worthy charities.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.510
To date, his organization
Sound Waves Art Foundation

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.800
has raised nearly $7
million, which is incredible.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.220
When they were here,
he debuted a new piece,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.170
the image of my song
"Broken and Beautiful,"

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.618
which is actually written by P!nk.

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:36.690
(audience applauding)

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.520
P!nk and I both signed the piece,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.610
and I'm so excited to say
it was bought for $50,000

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.690
at auction with the proceeds
going to No Kid Hungry.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.970
We have Tim on the line
right now to tell us more.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:48.803
What's up Tim?

00:00:48.803 --> 00:00:49.863
Nice to see you again.

00:00:50.857 --> 00:00:51.690
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.263
Hi Kelly, happy birthday.

00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:54.140
- Thank you, thank you so much.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.240
So you met the woman who
bought the piece, right?

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.073
- Oh, incredible.

00:00:58.073 --> 00:01:00.450
So she, yeah, as you
said, she bid $50,000,

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.860
so we thought the least we could do

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.780
is fly her down from Atlanta.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.580
So we brought her to, there she is,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.680
we brought her to Lockhart, Texas.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.850
And we took her to barbecue,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.550
and then we showed we
unveiled her artwork for her

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.087
and her partner.

00:01:13.087 --> 00:01:16.450
And to say it was emotional
would be an understatement.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.780
One of the best moments of my career.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.570
There's a lot of
expletives and swear words

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.520
that I couldn't possibly
repeat on your show,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.530
but it was fantastic.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.480
And, thanks to you and thanks to her,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:31.110
we've now raised over $60,000
in total for No Kid Hungry.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.853
- Wow.
- So that's amazing.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:34.943
- That's so incredible.

00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:36.270
And, I hear that you're actually embarking

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.650
on a new project right now, right?

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.090
- Yeah, we are.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.530
I mean, we couldn't do what we do

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.910
without the help of musicians.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.660
So, I think, as you say,
"It's time to pay it forward."

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.810
So, a lot of musicians,
I come from Austin, Texas

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.780
where we've got about 12,000
people in the industry.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.160
Many of them living on, you know,

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.100
beneath the poverty line
in the music industry.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.450
So we've got 24 local musicians
launching a collection

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.720
of artwork in May for Mental Health Month.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.740
And we are working with a
local charity called SIMS,

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.720
and we're gonna provide
mental health services

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.650
for musicians and people
in the music industry.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.180
And beyond that, we're gonna be working

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.570
with Sweet Relief Musicians
Fund who do a similar thing

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.585
on a national basis.

00:02:20.585 --> 00:02:22.860
And the good news is,
we're gonna now take this

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.000
to other music tens, starting
with Nashville in 2024.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.160
So, very exciting stuff.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.363
- Oh, that's incredible!

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.670
Congratulations, man,

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.350
and thank you so much
for all you're doing.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.216
I'm liking your post
right now, right, Tim?

00:02:36.216 --> 00:02:38.100
(audience cheering)

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.240
- [Tim] Oh, thank you so much.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.150
And we couldn't have done
it without your help,

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.300
so thank you so much.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.530
- Well, yeah, well that's not all,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.810
our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.150
the Go-To Erasable Pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.890
love how you're using art and music

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.900
to support all sorts of people in need.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.733
So in honor,

00:02:52.733 --> 00:02:56.100
they are giving Sweet Relief
Musicians Fund $1,000.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.488
How's that sound?

00:02:57.488 --> 00:02:58.321
(audience cheering)

00:02:58.321 --> 00:02:59.910
- Wow.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.380
- [Kelly] Thank you, Tim!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.970
And thank you to all our guests this hour

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.460
who celebrated my birthday
with me, Jimmy Allen,

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.430
the BoykinZ, Mikaela, Jude and Isaiah.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.660
I hope you're all having a great day.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.670
And thank you once again to
everybody who did a video,

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.810
that was very sweet.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.700
Jake Gyllenhaal, you're hilarious.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.800
If it's not a great day, y'all, change it.

